      "raw_text": "To solve this problem, we will follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the speed of the plane.**\nThe formula for speed is:\n$$ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} $$\n\nGiven:\n*   Distance traveled = $1200$ miles\n*   Time taken = $3$ hours\n\nSubstituting the values:\n$$ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1200}{3} = 400 \\text{ miles per hour} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the time required to travel the additional distance.**\nThe problem states the plane travels at the same rate. We need to find the time ($t$) it takes to travel an additional $2000$ miles at $400$ mph.\n\nThe formula for time is:\n$$ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} $$\n\nGiven:\n*   Additional Distance = $2000$ miles\n*   Speed = $400$ mph\n\nSubstituting the values:\n$$ t = \\frac{2000}{400} $$\n$$ t = 5 \\text{ hours} $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nIt would take 5 additional hours to travel the extra 2000 miles.\n\n#### 5<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To solve this problem, we will follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the speed of the plane.**\nThe formula for speed is:\n$$ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} $$\n\nGiven:\n*   Distance traveled = $1200$ miles\n*   Time taken = $3$ hours\n\nSubstituting the values:\n$$ \\text{Speed} = \\frac{1200}{3} = 400 \\text{ miles per hour} $$\n\n**Step 2: Calculate the time required to travel the additional distance.**\nThe problem states the plane travels at the same rate. We need to find the time ($t$) it takes to travel an additional $2000$ miles at $400$ mph.\n\nThe formula for time is:\n$$ \\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}} $$\n\nGiven:\n*   Additional Distance = $2000$ miles\n*   Speed = $400$ mph\n\nSubstituting the values:\n$$ t = \\frac{2000}{400} $$\n$$ t = 5 \\text{ hours} $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nIt would take 5 additional hours to travel the extra 2000 miles.\n\n#### 5",
